SlothClash core patch 0037: XHTTP packet-up keeps several uploads in flight.

mihomo waits for the response of every packet-up upload before it sends the
next one, so upload speed is capped at one sc-max-each-post-bytes per round
trip plus sc-min-posts-interval-ms. Like Xray's client, the writer now starts
an upload as soon as the previous request has been written and paces uploads
(not writes) by sc-min-posts-interval-ms. Uploads wait for their response in a
window of 8 seqs: seq N starts only once seq N-8 has been answered, so a
server never holds more than 7 uploads ahead of the one it waits for, within
the default sc-max-buffered-posts (30) of Xray, mihomo and Citrus. A failed
upload fails the next Write; Close lets the uploads in flight finish (up to
1 s) and then cancels them. With `alpn: [http/1.1]` every upload still waits
for its response (no multiplexing: each would hold a connection). The server
side is unchanged: mihomo's listener already puts uploads back in order by seq.

The seq window follows Rerowros/veles (v1.19.33-veles.3, commit f3d6ddaf,
transport/xhttp/client.go, GPL-3.0); waiting for the request write and the
HTTP/1.1 exception follow getmikan/Citrus (transport/xhttp/client.go,
GPL-3.0). Written for this tree; tests in packet_up_pipeline_test.go.

